      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Finite coefficient residue field, exact Z_l reduction and prime-to-ell torsion injectivity are proved at the original Coef scope; ell-primary torsion reduces to one."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE2",
      "block_sha256": "838673d6149822d742c937dc0ec2eeac649ed9eb0ebddad211cbb4a008af5978",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The modulus CRT projection and image-primary projection are distinguished and then matched to the original source formulas, conductors and kapB/kapL decomposition."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE3",
      "block_sha256": "f36b82cbfde602843108e10dd9d2c2b60f6342a7f7709cf7fc1cb86626844840",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The full cyclotomic inertia image and corrected Frobenius are constructed at every specified place. The ell case corrects Frobenius by inertia, and the other cases preserve the required residual cyclotomic value."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE4",
      "block_sha256": "85226557615c647fc35532bcc0034efd9a63f1222922a696c474c34f7c81b9e1",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The quadratic integral basis and discriminant square root give the exact sign character, including both congruence classes of the squarefree radicand."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE5",
      "block_sha256": "1fb0585290c1060502de17150f7f28da112e5ba1a7a2fa172d89f71c41222913",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Quadratic Gauss sums, i and sqrt(2) give the precise discriminant cyclotomic containment and the inertia consequence at ell prime to the discriminant."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE6",
      "block_sha256": "919d3eb004704f40b15dd8d1f4b6090d84337b17afeea1ccfdf018924fc29bd0",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "One inertia exponent is chosen before all places. The original GD kernel and weight guard supply g4 and g5 without an extra nondegeneracy hypothesis."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE7",
      "block_sha256": "d07d6ac04692644ddbe87d890e9dc5f736b8affcf77424de4d371c434302b747",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "All nineteen Gen fields are checked for Dat with Hb=top and M=ell*N*abs(disc K), retaining full original characters and the specified valuation."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE8",
      "block_sha256": "3ed0beedfc07b0ad0b3f7dc7de30db4e7125809a7ca6d468d3c12408906c8ad6",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The actual dyadic conductor at least four forces the Host kernel obstruction; the element is adjusted to be minus one modulo four and in the character kernel."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE9",
      "block_sha256": "a41fd12ab5aa03f97af11f0dc8fa193240ed1488afb5a449a53e84c972f7edcf",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The dyadic principal-unit order calculation uses the actual conductor and the strict numerical bound to prove the required nonquadratic value, with all exponents accounted for."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE10",
      "block_sha256": "adb329e6fe1f8062a9134942f76ec39a3e70332a30b8580086319ce9f83cd682",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "A witness is produced at every p in Tb and every chosen valuation. Squaring fixes eta4, preserves the cyclotomic kernel and keeps the squared residual character nontrivial, including ell=3."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE11",
      "block_sha256": "d71360f049f2994998a2544607850fa02672a8bb6381cb15def8d254b382220e",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The actual subgroup ker(dirG(kapB)) is open, abelian and of ell-power index, contains ell inertia and gives the full away-from-ell Teichmuller implication."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE12",
      "block_sha256": "c7e1a069bbd3bb2ca937d38112f55433f3e740d0fb82a9458e0145d45aede035",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "All nineteen Host Gen fields hold with the literal subgroup and M=ell*N. The Host branch does not inherit the stronger Dat prime guard."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE13",
      "block_sha256": "ae97825d49769e4d401eb27101c1ddb2ed810d23ce338fd6e80ad07e9dbc245c",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "All ten IsHostFrame fields are constructed on the actual GS quotient, with the original places, inertia groups, sign, character and complex conjugation; P is unnecessary."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE14",
      "block_sha256": "6eb93d5196fcbef884cc35d9336fcec1e50aa26f0b12b53bba33d3280ada56a7",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The full exists_sigma statement is proved on any supplied original Host frame and at every allowed index; the character residue field and exact local witness are retained."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE15",
      "block_sha256": "ed7b709e60e0f6e479532cf428cf7d1dd34832076a8a305535418767bbe9f206",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The full P-to-GdFrameEx join chooses the CAF modulus Q before L and w and uses the same LFC marked g1, frame and C0, including the actual SeedClause."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE16",
      "block_sha256": "fe15b645bd3731ad6af01103c7b0abdc503f6d3cb9b717b920033480ba058d9b",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The full P-to-HostFrameEx join preserves that same choice order, actual Host subgroup and ell=3 scope."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE17",
      "block_sha256": "ecbe5ecbf1a74403a82d0f76d08656c87fc9d4308f93323eccc9e040c7140354",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "All five Marks conditions hold on the same chosen g1; the residual square inequality gives the required unit in the original local coefficient ring."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE18",
      "block_sha256": "29754708380bc772697d81f485fbb2c1351080756f285d85403021b81942ab14",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "Local ordinary characters are transported through the actual conjugation and local group map. The ordered three-factor zero product follows from the preserved standard flag, with the rightmost factor acting first."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE19",
      "block_sha256": "eeb6b50e198ae07eca4e293dc6ad1320e49bdadeea85b8eb633f8de3a5604419",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The full exists_nrep3 is proved for arbitrary original local O and local Noetherian domain A. The actual kernel closure, adic continuity, polarization, residual lift and inertia character formula are retained; neither completeness nor flatness is added."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE20",
      "block_sha256": "1839e5085486ce1a969264628b808843392a404b86db4c437546af7e6109a27d",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The whole FinPt-to-FinEnd theorem chooses G_L before every later coefficient algebra and ordinary point. The residue map and exact NRep character formula give the original characteristic polynomial on that one subgroup."
    },
    {
      "id": "AFE21",
      "block_sha256": "ef709c3b87cef0fc0d692bccabd5f70c1a39060233952976f4e2dffc3a11fd07",
      "status": "PASS",
      "review_note": "The same marked frame carries Marks and the conditional finite endpoint. P, FinPt, both automorphic seed producers and AutEnd/patching remain explicit; no full GdEnd or selected global closure is claimed."
    }
